From 5a240627d14823da6445ca8c2bf9204ec0912ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:41:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): one NC file per operation

A post option "Output", next to the Post picker: "One program" (the
default - the combined program is byte-identical, every golden stays)
or "One file per operation", which writes each program operation as
its own standalone program into a folder.

- Files are <program>_<nn>_<op>.<ext>: the project's stem (program
  when unsaved), nn in program order, names cut to portable
  characters; the extension is the script's own manifest entry.
- Each op's own stream (posting::op_streams, the pieces the combined
  stream is joined from) posts alone, so each file has the dialect's
  header and units, its own tool change, the safe start (G90, work
  offset, cancels, spindle and coolant for that op) and its own end
  (coolant off, M5, home, M30). Suppressed ops write no file.
- O-numbers: the engine publishes programNumber before onOpen (1 for a
  whole job); Fanuc, Mazak and Fanuc Lathe write O0001, O0002... per
  file.
- One refusal refuses all: the program gate runs once, every op's post
  must come back warning-free, and only then are the files written -
  to a scratch folder in the target, then renamed into place.
- PostOptions gains per_op, switched by the undoable SetPostOptions;
  saved as a top-level per_op_files key written only when on.
- UI: the Post action asks for a folder when per-op is chosen.

Fixes #111

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
